ol by mixing water with fats.", "LAXANTES QUE AUMENTAN EL BOLO INTESTINAL:Laxatives that increase intestinal bulk, like methylcellulose and psyllium, absorb water to enhance stool volume.", "DRA. JULIA ÁLVAREZ:Dra. Julia Álvarez is a medical professional who supports the development of young endocrinologists and initiatives in the medical field.", "LEOPOLDO GARCÍA-VALDECASAS:D. Leopoldo García-Valdecasas is a dedicated member of a team that has contributed to a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. He plays an active role in supporting daily medical initiatives, demonstrating his commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this important area of health.", "GLORIA GÓMEZ-PORTEIRO:Gloria Gómez-Porteiro is a dedicated team member actively involved in the development of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. She contributes significantly to the chapter's medical initiatives, playing a crucial role in advancing its objectives and promoting awareness in this important area of health.", "ISABEL HIGUERA PULGAR:Isabel Higuera Pulgar is a contributor who played a significant role in the creation of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. She is part of the team that collaborated on this chapter and actively supports various medical initiatives related to the field.", "ANA PRIETO:Ana Prieto is a dedicated contributor involved in the creation of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. As a team member, she plays a significant role in supporting daily medical efforts, demonstrating her commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this important area of health.", "MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL HUMANO:", "SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE PROBIÓTICOS Y PREBIÓTICOS:The Sociedad Española de Probióticos y Prebióticos is an organization focused on the scientific evidence of probiotics and prebiotics in health.", "NUTRICIÓN EN PATOLOGÍA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO:\"NUTRICIÓN EN PATOLOGÍA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO\" encompasses a comprehensive examination of nutrition as it relates to various pathologies of the digestive tract. This section emphasizes dietary recommendations specifically tailored for patients suffering from inflammatory bowel disease (EII), addressing the critical role of nutritional management in these cases. It discusses both enteral and parenteral nutrition methods, which are essential for patients facing intestinal issues. Additionally, the content highlights the importance of nutrition in the context of surgical patients and explores various studies and findings that underscore the significance of nutritional management in clinical settings. Overall, the focus is on how effective nutritional strategies can mitigate malnutrition and deficiencies that arise from digestive tract diseases, thereby promoting better gastrointestinal health.", "HILTON C:Hilton C is a co-author of a study on the variation of bowel habits in two population samples published in the British Medical Journal.", "IRVINE G:Irvine G is a co-author of a study on the variation of bowel habits in two population samples published in the British Medical Journal."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}